    "notes": "The staged result satisfies all four rules at once: `{ExampleSWC, ExampleRun}` is mapped to at most one task; the runnable's 10 ms timing event is a positive integer multiple of the 5 ms task period; `partition: \"PARTITION0\"` resolves to the declared `PARTITION0` partition, which is on the declared `CORE0` core, and 1200us / 10 ms + 400us / 5 ms = 20% stays inside its 70% threshold; and the sequence names one task with an ordered subsequence of that task's runnables. `period` is in seconds and `wcet` carries its own unit — the standard's two time forms, a period and a budget, coexist deliberately, and discovery publishes `period`'s unit so a client never has to infer it."
